  "notes": "GAAP city. Governmental lines from the governmental funds Statement of Revenues, Expenditures and Changes in Fund Balances Total column (p6-7); business-type lines from the proprietary funds Statement of Revenues, Expenses and Changes in Net Position Totals column (p10, five funds: Light, Water, Sewer, Compactor, Orner Apartments); business-type expense lines split by column: Orner Apartments column (28,563) as housing, the utility funds as utilities. Balance sheet is the government-wide Statement of Net Position Total column (p1-2). Miscellaneous 320,388 split into General Fund 303,195 (p14) and Keno 17,193 (p15); other governmental fund revenue is Keno only. Interest on governmental funds statement 9,014 is General Fund. 'General taxes' treated as property tax (no breakdown printed). Sales Tax Fund has no detail schedule (82,602 revenue, 27,525 community development). Detail: p14 combining General Fund schedule recorded by department column (supersedes the all-funds budget schedule p13 for governmental lines); the p13 budgetary-basis all-funds schedule is used only for the business-type disbursement lines (no totals recorded since the schedule mixes funds and a different basis). Combined transfers: gov in 96,500 and out 90,500 net +6,000 offsets business-type transfers out of 6,000 (Compactor). Reconciles: 537,022 + 861,972 - 817,450 + 96,500 - 90,500 = 587,544. Business: 2,056,614 + 917,360 - 925,379 - 6,000 = 2,042,595. ending_cash is governmental funds balance sheet cash and cash equivalents 574,138 + cash with county treasurer 2,514 = 576,652; ending_investments is certificates of deposit 20,352. Trimmed p12 (proprietary cash flow reconciliation of operating income, added by the v8 re-trim) adds no new fields; its net cash from operations 89,190 matches proprietary.operating. Read pages 1-15 of 15."
}